               + 'to its accounts office \u2014 each has its own standing and starts neutral. '
               + 'Inheritance is a rule about fiction, and it is not this page\u2019s to invent '
               + 'on your behalf.' },

            { t: 'head', v: 'What this connects to' },
            { t: 'links', v: [
                { to: 'build', tab: 'orgs', label: 'Build \u203a Factions',
                  sub: 'Making several at once, with the world already in mind.' },
                { to: 'map', label: 'World',
                  sub: 'Where the factions physically are.' }
            ] }
        ]
    },

    build: {
        title: 'Build',
        lead: 'The pipeline that turns an idea into a world: a premise, a charter, and then the '
            + 'records themselves, a kind at a time.',
        blocks: [
            { t: 'head', v: 'One route, several stages' },
            { t: 'p', v: 'Premise and Charter come first because everything after them is written '
                + 'against what they said. Then the world itself, then the kinds \u2014 places, '
                + 'species, factions, cast, items, threads \u2014 and an opening scene last.' },
            { t: 'p', v: 'The strip at the top is two different things depending on where you '
