                + 'thing it describes.' },

            { t: 'head', v: 'What this connects to' },
            { t: 'links', v: [
                { to: 'map', label: 'World',
                  sub: 'Where committed places land, and how they are arranged afterwards.' },
                { to: 'scene', label: 'Scene',
                  sub: 'Where the opening scene puts you.' },
                { to: 'settings', tab: 'world', label: 'Settings \u203a World',
                  sub: 'The vocabulary the pipeline writes into.' }
            ] }
        ]
    },

    settings: {
        title: 'Settings',
        lead: 'Two different kinds of thing live here, and it is worth knowing which is which: '
            + 'what your WORLD is made of, and how the ENGINE behaves. The first six tabs are '
            + 'the world; the last two are the engine.',
        blocks: [
            { t: 'head', v: 'The tabs' },
            { t: 'defs', v: [
                { k: 'World', v: 'Vocabulary \u2014 species, relationship archetypes, conditions, '
                    + 'and what gets added to the lorebook. The things a story IS.' },
                { k: 'Context', v: 'What is actually sent: the cast list, the world outline, what '
                    + 'is left out of each, and a preview of the real built text rather than a '
                    + 'description of it.' },
                { k: 'States', v: 'Every number a character or a situation can carry, and what it '
                    + 'reads as at each step. The creation door for health, stamina, approaches, '
